{"identifier":"JoanAvoi1947","title":"Joan Avoids a Cold","description":"How young children must behave to avoid transmitting germs to one another.","videoUrl":"https://archive.org/download/JoanAvoi1947/JoanAvoi1947_512kb.mp4","thumbnailUrl":"https://archive.org/services/img/JoanAvoi1947","sourcePageUrl":"https://archive.org/details/JoanAvoi1947","durationMs":615001,"level":"C2","topic":"Health and hygiene","sourceCredit":"Source: Internet Archive — Joan Avoids a Cold","hasCaptions":true,"segments":[{"startMs":22000,"endMs":29000,"text":"The guardians of our health, our doctors, nurses, teachers, teachers and parents are working together to keep us well."},{"startMs":29000,"endMs":35000,"text":"All of them must know and agree on the health practices we need at home, in the neighborhood and at school."},{"startMs":36000,"endMs":38000,"text":"This is Joan getting ready for school."},{"startMs":39000,"endMs":43001,"text":"Joan learned at school that it's important to choose the right clothes on a cold day."},{"startMs":44001,"endMs":48000,"text":"The temperature is 40, too cold for just a coat."},{"startMs":49001,"endMs":54000,"text":"She will need her snow suit if she wishes to keep well for the Dutch festival."},{"startMs":55000,"endMs":57001,"text":"And this is Jim, Joan's brother."},{"startMs":58001,"endMs":62000,"text":"They choose wraps to keep all of their body warm."},{"startMs":67000,"endMs":69001,"text":"Mother is the seed in Jim looking so well this morning."},{"startMs":70001,"endMs":75001,"text":"Their color is good, their eyes alert, they're ready for work or play."},{"startMs":76001,"endMs":81001,"text":"Mother needs to get another supply of paper handkerchiefs."},{"startMs":82001,"endMs":86000,"text":"Jim's friend George is eating an apple as he waits for them."},{"startMs":88000,"endMs":90000,"text":"That is a wise no thank you, Joan."},{"startMs":91000,"endMs":92000,"text":"Never share another's food."},{"startMs":94000,"endMs":98000,"text":"George has forgotten something, something that helps keep him clean."},{"startMs":99000,"endMs":102000,"text":"It's lucky for George that Joan has an extra tissue to lend him."},{"startMs":104000,"endMs":112001,"text":"Some children learn to jump or go around puddles, but George wades right into trouble because he forgot his galoshes."},{"startMs":115000,"endMs":117000,"text":"This is Miss May, Joan's teacher."},{"startMs":118000,"endMs":119001,"text":"George and Joan are glad to be in school."},{"startMs":120000,"endMs":122000,"text":"The children are getting ready for their Dutch festival."},{"startMs":123000,"endMs":128000,"text":"Tom has brought the thermometer in so that the children can guess what the weatherman doll should wear today."},{"startMs":128000,"endMs":131000,"text":"A raincoat and umbrella? Oh no."},{"startMs":131001,"endMs":134000,"text":"A snow suit and galoshes to keep him warm and dry."},{"startMs":134001,"endMs":138000,"text":"It was hard to guess today, but Tom is a good guesser."},{"startMs":138000,"endMs":140000,"text":"Or did Mother tell him what to wear?"},{"startMs":142000,"endMs":145000,"text":"George, you forgot something more important than your handkerchief."},{"startMs":145001,"endMs":150000,"text":"You forgot to cover your sneeze, and cold germs travel on your sneeze or cough, you know."},{"startMs":155000,"endMs":158001,"text":"Why cold germs can fly farther than Miss May can blow the feather."},{"startMs":159001,"endMs":163001,"text":"Cold germs can fly eight feet to another child's nose, hand, or food."},{"startMs":164001,"endMs":168001,"text":"People who put fingers into their mouths make it easy for cold germs to come to them."},{"startMs":171000,"endMs":172001,"text":"No, not that way, George."},{"startMs":173001,"endMs":177001,"text":"Blow your nose gently without pressing the opening of the nostrils closed."},{"startMs":179000,"endMs":179001,"text":"That's better."},{"startMs":181000,"endMs":184001,"text":"Oh, and your feet are wet. It's easy to catch cold when your body is chilly."},{"startMs":185000,"endMs":187001,"text":"You'd better go and see the school nurse. She'll help you."},{"startMs":189000,"endMs":191000,"text":"The nurse is examining Mary after her cold."},{"startMs":191001,"endMs":198001,"text":"Four days at home with the cold keeps others from catching it, and protects you from serious infections that follow colds."},{"startMs":199000,"endMs":201000,"text":"Now, George, who sent you in here?"},{"startMs":202000,"endMs":204001,"text":"Miss May said I might be catching a cold."},{"startMs":205000,"endMs":206001,"text":"Well, what do you think?"},{"startMs":207001,"endMs":208001,"text":"I'm hot and chilly."},{"startMs":209001,"endMs":213000,"text":"Well, did you sleep pretty well last night, and did you feel like getting up this morning?"},{"startMs":213001,"endMs":215000,"text":"Did your breakfast taste good?"},{"startMs":215001,"endMs":220001,"text":"I hardly had the time to have my breakfast. I had an apple on the way."},{"startMs":223000,"endMs":224001,"text":"Now, blow your nose, George."},{"startMs":226000,"endMs":229001,"text":"Oh, not so hard, gently. No pressure on the opening."},{"startMs":231001,"endMs":232001,"text":"Now, let's look at your throat."},{"startMs":238000,"endMs":241000,"text":"All right, now you sit down, and I'll take her."},{"startMs":241001,"endMs":244001,"text":"[...] loosen your lips and hold it under your tongue."},{"startMs":248001,"endMs":250001,"text":"Oh, your feet are wet too, George."},{"startMs":254001,"endMs":256000,"text":"The neck is three, two, one."},{"startMs":258000,"endMs":260000,"text":"Hello, is it Mrs. Powell there?"},{"startMs":260001,"endMs":261000,"text":"[...]"},{"startMs":261001,"endMs":263000,"text":"Well, this is Miss Wright, Mrs. Powell."},{"startMs":264000,"endMs":266001,"text":"George came in to see me a few moments ago with a cold."},{"startMs":268000,"endMs":271000,"text":"Yes, his throat is quite red, and his feet are wet too."},{"startMs":272000,"endMs":274001,"text":"I do think he'd be more comfortable at home in bed."},{"startMs":276000,"endMs":277000,"text":"Well, just a minute, please."},{"startMs":281001,"endMs":284000,"text":"Yes, his temperature is 998."},{"startMs":285001,"endMs":291000,"text":"Well, it isn't best to consult your physician if it goes over 100, especially during the cold season."},{"startMs":292001,"endMs":294001,"text":"Oh, that would be nice of you to call for him."},{"startMs":295000,"endMs":297000,"text":"Yes, he'll be right here in my office."},{"startMs":297001,"endMs":299000,"text":"Thank you so much. Goodbye."},{"startMs":302000,"endMs":304001,"text":"Joan's mother visits school to plan a health program."},{"startMs":305001,"endMs":309000,"text":"Joan must learn to take responsibility for keeping herself well."},{"startMs":309001,"endMs":315001,"text":"This weather chart keeps Joan alert to weather changes as she marks snowy or rainy days."},{"startMs":318001,"endMs":323001,"text":"Dressing this weather doll for outdoor weather helps Joan know what to wear herself."},{"startMs":324001,"endMs":330001,"text":"It will be better for mother when Joan chooses wraps to shoot the temperature instead of arguing about what friends wear."},{"startMs":333001,"endMs":335001,"text":"Mother and teacher check Joan's health habits."},{"startMs":336000,"endMs":339000,"text":"They plan better health practices for home and school."},{"startMs":340000,"endMs":345000,"text":"At school, Joan's committee keeps the washroom attractive with soap sponges, brushes, and signs."},{"startMs":345000,"endMs":350000,"text":"Others keep the closets neat, with boxes for rubbers and hangers for clothes."},{"startMs":351000,"endMs":355000,"text":"Another records the temperature and tells us when we need heat or fresh air."},{"startMs":358000,"endMs":362000,"text":"One group keeps large drawing pencils scrubbed ready for use."},{"startMs":362001,"endMs":365001,"text":"Those are jobs Joan and Jim could be learning to do at home, too."},{"startMs":366000,"endMs":368001,"text":"On Saturdays, they'll have to help us plan what we're going to do."},{"startMs":369001,"endMs":371001,"text":"I'm so glad to get this health record sheet."},{"startMs":372001,"endMs":377000,"text":"Your check on Joan's habits at school will help me plan a corrective health program at home."},{"startMs":378000,"endMs":385001,"text":"I'm going to find out what kind of health practices we use, and I must check on our equipment to see if we have the materials to carry on the school practices."},{"startMs":386001,"endMs":389000,"text":"Thank you for some grand ideas, Miss May."},{"startMs":389000,"endMs":392000,"text":"I'm going to visit school again some afternoon when I call for Joan."},{"startMs":392001,"endMs":393000,"text":"May I?"},{"startMs":394001,"endMs":395001,"text":"Do come often."},{"startMs":396000,"endMs":400001,"text":"It is good for teachers and children to have parents visit school."},{"startMs":403001,"endMs":407001,"text":"Next morning, Joan's mother is inspecting the health materials in her home."},{"startMs":408000,"endMs":411001,"text":"Each one in the family needs a separate towel and washcloth."},{"startMs":412000,"endMs":416000,"text":"Mother has one for Jim and another for Joan, each with his own name."},{"startMs":417001,"endMs":420000,"text":"Joan's father made a box for her to stand on."},{"startMs":420000,"endMs":423001,"text":"It's no fun washing if you have to stretch or can't see into the basin."},{"startMs":425000,"endMs":426000,"text":"And here are new cups."},{"startMs":427000,"endMs":428001,"text":"Each can have his own cup now."},{"startMs":429000,"endMs":430001,"text":"It prevents catching another's cold."},{"startMs":431000,"endMs":433001,"text":"A gym. Why are you so cross?"},{"startMs":436001,"endMs":439000,"text":"Father has taught Joan to spit into the toilet."},{"startMs":439000,"endMs":441000,"text":"For spitting spreads disease."},{"startMs":443001,"endMs":446000,"text":"Here are the spoons for your cod liver oil, Joan."},{"startMs":446001,"endMs":449001,"text":"It's extra sunshine for us in winter and spring."},{"startMs":450001,"endMs":458000,"text":"You know, strong bodies can't always keep us from catching cold, but they help us resist a serious illness that may follow colds."},{"startMs":458000,"endMs":463000,"text":"Keep away from persons with colds and keep your hands clean while you're eating."},{"startMs":466000,"endMs":476000,"text":"Jim must wash his hands after he pets his dog, but he won't have to go upstairs, as Father has arranged a wash stand downstairs so Jim will remember to wash."},{"startMs":478000,"endMs":479000,"text":"What's the trouble with Jim?"},{"startMs":480000,"endMs":483001,"text":"He didn't like his breakfast and he was restless as he slept."},{"startMs":484000,"endMs":486000,"text":"He's cross and tired this morning."},{"startMs":487000,"endMs":491000,"text":"His throat isn't very red, but his eyes look queer."},{"startMs":492000,"endMs":495000,"text":"He better stay home today so that Mother can watch him and keep him warm."},{"startMs":496001,"endMs":501000,"text":"Joan's Mother can't go to the Kermis now, so Joan must take the paper bags for the party."},{"startMs":502001,"endMs":505000,"text":"Colds are easy to catch during the first 24 hours."},{"startMs":505001,"endMs":509000,"text":"Mother must see that Jim covers his coughs and stays away from others."},{"startMs":509001,"endMs":512001,"text":"She must sterilize his dishes by boiling them thoroughly in water."},{"startMs":514000,"endMs":522000,"text":"Joan's room at school is a busy place, and Joan wants to help get ready for the Kermis, but first she must wash her hands."},{"startMs":523001,"endMs":528001,"text":"We must always wash hands clean before handling food."},{"startMs":529001,"endMs":534000,"text":"So, Joan takes off a coat, uses plenty of soap and a good lather."},{"startMs":535000,"endMs":538001,"text":"She rinses her hands well and dries them thoroughly with a paper towel."},{"startMs":540001,"endMs":544001,"text":"In another room, the kindergarten children are getting ready for the Kermis."},{"startMs":545000,"endMs":548000,"text":"It's best to go to the toilet and wash hands first."},{"startMs":549001,"endMs":555000,"text":"Now Joan has her wraps off, her hands are clean, and she's ready to pack the bags for the Kermis."},{"startMs":557000,"endMs":559000,"text":"The Kermis has started."},{"startMs":560000,"endMs":562000,"text":"George's friends are selling the flowers they raised."},{"startMs":562001,"endMs":572000,"text":"They learn that flowers, like children, need plenty of sunshine, water, good food, and moderate temperature to make them grow."},{"startMs":573000,"endMs":577000,"text":"Joan's friends are selling cheese, and they are careful to keep the food clean."},{"startMs":577001,"endMs":582001,"text":"Everyone is having a good time while poor George stays in bed."},{"startMs":583000,"endMs":588001,"text":"His careless habits have made Jim miss the Kermis too, and Jim is restless in bed."},{"startMs":588001,"endMs":592001,"text":"Now he knows it pays to avoid people with colds."},{"startMs":592001,"endMs":597000,"text":"But Jim's friends are enjoying the Kermis. They learn that Dutch people are clean."},{"startMs":597001,"endMs":601001,"text":"Hollanders leave their wooden shoes on their doorstep so that their floors are spotless."},{"startMs":602000,"endMs":606001,"text":"The Dutch drink milk and raise their own vegetables and flowers. They keep well."},{"startMs":608000,"endMs":610001,"text":"You have seen these children learning to take care of themselves."},{"startMs":611001,"endMs":615001,"text":"Now, do you know why George and Jim missed the Kermis?"}]}